ironment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:89db247e5c0211d675ea33e7b748dcf8c0b522c57eb35a572112901dc7850e53","file":"preprints/A-two-dimensional-area-law-from-a-global-spectral-gap-September-24-2026/build/sections/00-introduction.tex","line":69,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"d44d97f7c7d122fe2c7e8f942678f6f5b53bd766b4b9426525115cf1b50478ef","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/A-two-dimensional-area-law-from-a-global-spectral-gap-September-24-2026/build/sections/00-introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:89db247e5c0211d675ea33e7b748dcf8c0b522c57eb35a572112901dc7850e53","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/A-two-dimensional-area-law-from-a-global-spectral-gap-September-24-2026/build/sections/00-introduction.tex#L69"},"statement_kind":"corollary","text":"\\label{cor:rectangles}\nThe conclusion of Theorem~\\ref{thm:area} holds for every subset of a finite\nrectangular square lattice with bounded on-site and nearest-neighbor\ninteractions and a unique ground state separated by a fixed global gap.\nFor every domain covered by that theorem it also implies\n\\[\n S_\\Omega(A)\\le4C|\\partial_{\\rm in}A|,\n \\qquad S_\\Omega(A)\\le2C|Z_A|.\n\\]"}
